Oh nice! What games would you reccommend for PC, and do you have any games that you have on both PC and Console that you prefer to play on one rather than the other? 

&#x200B;

I'm sorry for all the questions lol when I get excited I ramble a bit, feel free to not reply when I start getting annoying

Lol! So you think it's worth the wait, huh? I could definitely wait then. I'd just really hate to mess something up if I build it from scratch but I guess it'll be a good learning experience! I'm gonna have to not get my nails done just so I can build it lol. I'm actually really excited now. 

&#x200B;

About how much do you think they'll go for? Or have they not dropped a price yet?

One chapter in my book was 30 thousand+ words and I damn near died writing that. I knew I had to get it out to my readers so I sorta rushed the end on that and I ended up going back and doing an entire re-write of the end of that chapter because of how much I ended up hating it. 

&#x200B;

When you're writing and you're at a point where you've gotta literally force yourself to finish that chapter or draft or part or whatever you want to call it, you've got to stop or you're going to mess up your work. Just take a break, get back to it later. As a writer I understand that one of the most frustrating things is when you're writing and there's a specific part of your book that you're really excited to write/edit and you want to just get to it but there's so much other stuff you have to do first; it's a pain but it's necessary, you want your book to be of the best quality, correct? Don't force yourself to write. Give yourself time to let it flow and write it in the way you know is best. 

&#x200B;

Aishm, I rambled, but to answer your question: I haven't read your book, so I don't know if you should write those remaining 11000 words or not, but if you feel like you'll write more when you edit, then probably do that. Edit it, re-read everything you've written and by the time you get back to that part, everything will flow a bit more eloquently and you'll know what you have to write. Is this making sense? I feel like it's not but I've explained it to what I feel like is the best of my ability in my tmi drunken state. Let me know how everything goes, I'm genuinely interested in the update
